# civ-rag API requests
#
# Requires the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request"
# above any request below.
#
# The API key is read from .env (gitignored), so nothing secret lives in this
# file and it is safe to commit.
#
# Cost note: /health and /warm are both free of model tokens. /health is the
# safe one to hammer; /warm opens a Neon connection, so it is key-gated.
# /query spends Bedrock tokens on every call, so use it deliberately.
#
# Cold start: the first call after an image push can take ~23s and API Gateway
# gives up at 30s. Call /warm first, then /query. NOTE this changed: /health no
# longer warms anything. Agent construction moved out of the FastAPI lifespan
# into the get_agent() singleton, which made /health genuinely dependency-free
# (correct for a liveness probe) and left /warm as the only route that builds
# the agent and wakes the database.

@aws = https://uijw31ulv5.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
@local = http://localhost:8000

### AWS health check (dependency-free; does NOT warm)
GET {{aws}}/health

### AWS warm (builds the agent, wakes Neon, no Bedrock tokens)
POST {{aws}}/warm
X-API-Key: {{$dotenv API_SHARED_SECRET}}

### AWS query (spends Bedrock tokens)
POST {{aws}}/query
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{$dotenv API_SHARED_SECRET}}

{
  "query": "What does the Eagle Warrior do?",
  "thread_id": "smoke-test",
  "history": []
}

### Local health check (dependency-free; does NOT warm)
# Start the service first:
#   uv run --extra api uvicorn src.api:app --port 8000
GET {{local}}/health

### Local warm (builds the agent, no Bedrock tokens)
POST {{local}}/warm
X-API-Key: {{$dotenv API_SHARED_SECRET}}

### Local query
POST {{local}}/query
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{$dotenv API_SHARED_SECRET}}

{
  "query": "What does the Eagle Warrior do?",
  "thread_id": "smoke-test",
  "history": []
}
